{"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1776109,"title":"File:Bubo bubo portrait.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Bubo_bubo_portrait.jpg/960px-Bubo_bubo_portrait.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bubo_bubo_portrait.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"A Eurasian Eagle Owl (<i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Bubo_bubo\" title=\"Bubo bubo\">Bubo bubo</a></i>)."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2007-03-10"},"Artist":{"value":"Flickr user <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/indygnome/\">indygnome</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0"}}}]},{"pageid":2204433,"title":"File:Buchenwald Slave Laborers Liberation.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Buchenwald_Slave_Laborers_Liberation.jpg/960px-Buchenwald_Slave_Laborers_Liberation.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buchenwald_Slave_Laborers_Liberation.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"These are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unfree_labour\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Unfree labour\">slave laborers</a> in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buchenwald_concentration_camp\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Buchenwald concentration camp\">Buchenwald concentration camp</a> near <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weimar\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Weimar\">Weimar</a>; many had died from malnutrition when U.S. troops of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/80th_Division_(United_States)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:80th Division (United States)\">80th Division</a> entered the camp.  The very ill man lying at the back on the lower bunk was thought to be <a href=\"https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Max_Hamburger\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"nl:Max Hamburger\">Max Hamburger</a>, but this is probably not true. Second row, seventh from left is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elie_Wiesel\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Elie Wiesel\">Elie Wiesel</a>. Photograph taken 5 days after rescue."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on 16 April 1945"},"Artist":{"value":"Private H. Miller. (Army)"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain"}}}]},{"pageid":3903482,"title":"File:Buchenwald-bei-Weimar-am-24-April-1945.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Buchenwald-bei-Weimar-am-24-April-1945.jpg/960px-Buchenwald-bei-Weimar-am-24-April-1945.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buchenwald-bei-Weimar-am-24-April-1945.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Senator <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alben_W._Barkley\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Alben W. Barkley\">Alben W. Barkley</a> of Kentucky, a member of a congressional committee investigating Nazi atrocities, views the evidence at first hand at Buchenwald concentration camp. Weimar, Germany."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on 24 April 1945"},"Artist":{"value":"Unknown<span style=\"display: none;\">Unknown </span> soldier of the US Army"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain"}}}]},{"pageid":6488843,"title":"File:Buckingham Palace, London - April 2009.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Buckingham_Palace%2C_London_-_April_2009.jpg/960px-Buckingham_Palace%2C_London_-_April_2009.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buckingham_Palace,_London_-_April_2009.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Buckingham Palace in London, England. taken by myself with a Canon 5D and 24-105mm f/4L IS lens.